-TEX-I-1D461\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2161,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(809,-345) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(523,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D461\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D461\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"2003.1\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is the rate of radioactive decay at time t. If the number of radioactive nuclei of this element decreases by a factor of p after 4.16 years, the value of p is __________.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l4bkvlqq/29a2d0e1-d019-4bf3-9f35-b21375354ad7/c0146230-ea74-11ec-a537-3baab2e403e6/file-1l4bkvlqr.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l4bkvlqq/29a2d0e1-d019-4bf3-9f35-b21375354ad7/c0146230-ea74-11ec-a537-3baab2e403e6/file-1l4bkvlqr.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Atoms and Nuclei Question 27 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l4bkvlqq/29a2d0e1-d019-4bf3-9f35-b21375354ad7/c0146230-ea74-11ec-a537-3baab2e403e6/file-1l4bkvlqr.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l4bkvlqq/29a2d0e1-d019-4bf3-9f35-b21375354ad7/c0146230-ea74-11ec-a537-3baab2e403e6/file-1l4bkvlqr.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l4bkvlqq/29a2d0e1-d019-4bf3-9f35-b21375354ad7/c0146230-ea74-11ec-a537-3baab2e403e6/file-1l4bkvlqr.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l4bkvlqq/29a2d0e1-d019-4bf3-9f35-b21375354ad7/c0146230-ea74-11ec-a537-3baab2e403e6/file-1l4bkvlqr.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/